# FABLE-SONNET-EMPTY-STRUCT-20260923-132: a hanging, unclosed `f:` is not
# one of the three empty-Structure spellings -- P0 refuses it (error 32,
# "empty colon Frame is not allowed") before the translator ever sees a
# Frame to recognize. Grok's -127 P0 parity unified `f()`, `f: ()` and the
# CLOSED empty vertical into one tree; a bare `f:` with no closing `---`
# and no body stays outside that, same as before.
fn: probe () int
    mystruct:
    return: 0
end: probe

return: probe()
